{"segs": ["PA_ja_239:0.4", "PA_ja_239:1.1"], "en": "9. The Jātaka of the Green Frog “Even though I am a venomous snake,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_239:1.2"], "en": "having entered the mouth of the fish-trap;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_239:1.3", "PA_ja_239:1.4"], "en": "\"It pleases the mother of the green ones that these fish eat me.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_239:2.1"], "en": "\"A man indeed plunders,\" [said the other].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_239:2.2"], "en": "As long as it serves him;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_239:2.3", "PA_ja_239:2.4"], "en": "but when others plunder him, he, being plundered, plunders in turn.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
